# Phase 17 --- CodeBuild YAML Troubleshooting

An initial build failed with an error similar to:

``` text
Expected Commands[] to be of string type
```

The cause was invalid YAML structure under `commands`.

Correct structure:

``` yaml
commands:
  - echo "Building..."
  - docker build -t $IMAGE_URI .
  - docker push $IMAGE_URI
```

Each item under `commands` must be a command string.

After correcting `buildspec.yml`, CodeBuild completed successfully.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Phase 18 --- EKS CrashLoopBackOff Troubleshooting

During an early deployment, the Pod entered:

``` text
CrashLoopBackOff
```

Pod logs showed:

``` text
exec /docker-entrypoint.sh: exec format error
```

The container image architecture was investigated.

The EKS worker node was:

``` text
amd64
```

while the Docker image was built as:

``` text
linux/arm64
```

This produced an architecture mismatch:

``` text
Docker image
linux/arm64
      X
      |
      v
EKS node
linux/amd64
```

The image was rebuilt for the correct architecture.

Example:

``` bash
docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 -t <ECR_URI>:<TAG> --push .
```

A multi-platform image can also be built:

``` bash
docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64 -t <ECR_URI>:<TAG> --push .
```

The important principle is:

``` text
Docker image architecture
          |
          v
must be compatible with
          |
          v
EKS node architecture
```

After correcting the image architecture, the application successfully
started on EKS.

