# Phase 21 --- CloudWatch IAM and Pod Identity

Fluent Bit runs inside EKS and needs AWS permissions to send logs to
CloudWatch.

A dedicated IAM role was created:

``` text
EKS-CloudWatch-Agent-Role
```

The AWS-managed policy attached to the role is:

``` text
CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy
```

An EKS Pod Identity association connects:

``` text
Namespace:
amazon-cloudwatch

Service Account:
cloudwatch-agent
```

to:

``` text
EKS-CloudWatch-Agent-Role
```

The resulting flow is:

``` text
EKS
 |
 +--> Fluent Bit
       |
       | Pod Identity
       v
EKS-CloudWatch-Agent-Role
       |
       v
CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy
       |
       v
CloudWatch Logs
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Phase 22 --- CloudWatch Troubleshooting

Initially Fluent Bit produced:

``` text
AccessDeniedException
Failed to create log stream
Failed to send events
```

This showed that the CloudWatch workload did not have sufficient
permissions.

The problem was resolved by configuring:

1.  EKS Pod Identity agent
2.  IAM role
3.  CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy
4.  Pod Identity association

After the configuration, EKS application logs appeared in CloudWatch.

A temporary:

``` text
OperationAbortedException
```

was also observed during concurrent log-group creation. This is
different from `AccessDeniedException` and indicates a conflicting
CloudWatch resource operation rather than a missing IAM permission.

